APPEAL DECISION: OVERTURNED — FULL PAYMENT AUTHORIZED

After review of the clinical documentation submitted with your appeal, including the
operative record, nursing notes, and physician attestation, we have determined that
the original assignment of MS-DRG 291 (Heart Failure and Shock with MCC) was clinically
appropriate for this admission.

The initial DRG downgrade to MS-DRG 292 has been reversed. Full reimbursement at the
contracted rate for MS-DRG 291 will be processed.

PAYMENT DETAIL
Original Denied Amount (DRG differential): $4,210.00
Approved Amount: $4,210.00
Expected Payment: Within 30 days of this notice

WHAT HAPPENS NEXT
No further action is required on your part. Payment will be issued to Memorial Health
System via EFT within 30 days. A remittance advice will accompany the payment.

FINAL DETERMINATION
This is a final determination for this level of appeal. If you believe there are
additional clinical grounds for reconsideration, contact BCBS Provider Relations.

